From c07109e20de1bdd4208bbdd0f8668e5819ad77fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 15:18:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] iowave redesign phases 0-1: NHFLOW/FNPF regression cases,
 wave_field superposition

Phase 0
- regression_dump: exact state and per-step norms for the NHFLOW and FNPF
  driver loops (inactive unless REEF3D_REGRESSION_DIR is set; CFD results
  bitwise unchanged)
- regression.py: NHFLOW/FNPF text output and bulk folders
- 11 NHFLOW/FNPF wave cases (relaxation, Dirichlet, AWA, waves on a
  current, decomposed irregular, 3D short-crested, 2 ranks) with blessed
  references; irregular cases fix B 139 / B 138 seeds

Phase 1
- wave_source / wave_field: additional wave sources (B 500 id type H T,
  B 501 id dir phase ts te t_ramp, B 502 id x0 y0, B 504 id seed),
  superposed on the B 92 wave behind the unchanged wave_interface API
- each source wraps an unchanged wave_lib with its own copy of the lexer
  fields the libraries read and write
- without B 50x lines the old code path runs unchanged (13 phase 0 cases
  bitwise identical); two linear sources match the analytical sum
- setup checks: one nonlinear source at most, no B 89 1 / HDC / wavemaker
  with several sources
- 4 new cases (NHFLOW two sources, 2 ranks, irregular two sources, FNPF)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
