From 4e11cef2e7080cd91d43b7614f139d64d0b1e1c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 18:44:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] iowave redesign phase 2a, slice 1: bc_zone

- bc_zone / bc_zone_set: solver-agnostic boundary zones (reference line,
  half width, method, relaxation weight, distance, AMR box), translated
  from B 96 / B 98 / B 99 / B 107 / B 108 with the former iowave arithmetic
- iowave rb1_ext, rb1_flag, rb3_ext, distgen_calc, distbeach_calc
  delegate to the zone set (all solvers)
- nhflow_amr / fnpf_amr: no-refinement boxes from the zones instead of the
  hard-coded B 96 x-ranges, so B 107 / B 108 zones are respected as well
- REEF3D.project: add bc_zone, wave_field, wave_source
- regression: nhflow_3d_amr_relax, fnpf_3d_amr_relax (AMR active)
- bitwise identical to phase 1 on all 19 NHFLOW/FNPF cases and the 11
  CFD quick cases

Note: iowave::dist2 (used by iozonecheck) no longer follows the last
B 107 zone evaluated; it stays B 96 2, as for the default zone.

